// Repo context: what is true of this repository rather than of any image
// in it.
//
// Every other `.kdl` at the root is an image. This file is the one that is
// not, which is what makes "a file is an image" a rule with no exceptions
// to remember.
//
// The schema is documented in modules/SCHEMA.md.
// Nothing here reaches a build.

// Which image a build with no target named builds, and which one a pull
// request builds, by id rather than by file name. Both optional, and both
// pointless with one image: there is nothing to choose between. Declare
// `default-image` as soon as a second image exists, because a build has to
// be told, and the tie-break that would avoid saying so — first file
// alphabetically — would mean renaming a file changed what `just build`
// builds.
//
// default-image "falcos"
// pr-image "falcos"

// Optional. Which workflows in .github/workflows/ actually run, named by
// file stem, for a fork that wants the weekly smoke test off or has no
// registry to publish to.
//
// - enabled: #false switches the workflow off, #true switches it back on
//
// A workflow not named here runs, so an absent block is this repository as
// it ships, which is why nothing is declared below. Uncomment to turn one
// off:
//
// workflows {
//     smoke-test enabled=#false
// }
//
// Reconciled by .github/workflows/reconcile-workflows.yml through the
// GitHub API on every push to main that touches this file. Not by
// rewriting the workflow files: GITHUB_TOKEN cannot push under that path,
// so anything that edited them would need a PAT or a GitHub App, and a
// fork would have to provision a secret before it built at all. Nothing
// here reaches a build, so changing it does not regenerate a Containerfile.
//
// The reconciler is the one workflow that cannot be switched off from
// here: it skips itself, because disabling it would leave this block with
// nothing to act on it. Delete the file instead.
